// AN `@` IN A LITERAL, WHEREVER THE LITERAL STANDS (E-c of DEF-413, E-e of DEF-410 (c), and the form table of landing 177a; management_12's ruling of 2026-11-01 07:00: the class, not the next shape).
// `C:c = is (b) : C{ p: @h, k: (raw take(move(h.s))) } : C{ ... };` formed the address, vacated the field and read a fabricated length through the holder (`ec_main`, 60 on 175 and 176b); `??`, `?|`, a cast, a `Result` literal and a
// pick expression's `give` (`ec_pick`, 60) did the same; so did an argument or a receiver (`a_*`), and a template's piece (`l_tmpl_lit` 62, `l_tmpl_nested` 61, `l_tmpl_arg` 90). `value_arms` in alias.npk is ONE table
// of the 50 `ExprKind`s, what a node's value comes up through, with no `(*)`: a kind added later fails NITPICK-PICK-001 at the table and compiles nothing. Each stepped form has a case here; each form the table does not step is in 1.6.1e.md's table with its reason.
// E-e: an `@l[0]` under a literal froze nothing against a reallocation (`ee_main`, 239; `ee_lit_init`, 230): the same element-address party as the bare argument's. A move in one pick arm against `@h` in another is over-refused (`ee_rev_lit`), post-180.
mod:literal_addr_initialiser;
